{"step_index":172,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-01T14:16:56Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-01T19:46:56+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-11-01T19:46:57+05:30\nThe tool's output was truncated due to being too long. You can find the full output in a file at file:///C:/Users/int-vasanth/.gemini/antigravity/brain/a01f3378-859c-4460-83c1-fd265a9ee6b1/.system_generated/steps/172/output.txt.\n\nHere is a preview with the middle of the output truncated:\nCommand exited with code 0.\n\nCommand output:\n.env.example:MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://user:password@cluster.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority\nconversations/session_02_movie_bot_architecture_explained/.system_generated/logs/chunks/transcript/00000000.jsonl:{\"step_index\":25,\"source\":\"MODEL\",\"type\":\"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\"status\":\"DONE\",\"created_at\":\"2026-11-01T13:34:02Z\",\"input_tokens\":2543,\"cache_read_tokens\":27184,\"output_tokens\":804,\"tool_calls\":[{\"name\":\"write_file\",\"args\":{\"ArtifactMetadata\":\"{\\\"RequestFeedback\\\":false,\\\"Summary\\\":\\\"Step-by-step walkthrough to get Telegram Bot Token, Telegram API ID & Hash, Private Storage Channel, and Free MongoDB Atlas URI for the Hybrid Movie Bot.\\\",\\\"UserFacing\\\":true}\",\"Content\":\"\\\"# Telegram & MongoDB Credentials Setup Walkthrough\\\\n\\\\nThis guide details how to obtain the necessary credentials to build and run your **Hybrid Telegram Movie Bot**.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 1. Telegram Bot Token (@BotFather)\\\\n1. Open Telegram and search for **`@BotFather`**.\\\\n2. Send `/newbot`.\\\\n3. Provide a display name (e.g., `My Movie Streamer`) and a bot username ending in `bot` (e.g., `my_movie_streamer_bot`).\\\\n4. Copy the HTTP API token provided (e.g., `1234567890:ABCdefGhIJKlmNoPQRsTUVwxyZ`).\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 2. Telegram API ID & API Hash (my.telegram.org)\\\\n1. Navigate to [my.telegram.org](https://my.telegram.org) in a web browser.\\\\n2. Sign in with your Telegram phone number and verify via the in-app code.\\\\n3. Click on **API development tools**.\\\\n4. Fill in an app title and short name (e.g., `MovieScraper`).\\\\n5. Copy the generated **`App api_id`** and **`App api_hash`**.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 3. Private Storage / Log Channel\\\\\n<truncated 6221 bytes>\nisibility:** Public (recommended so the DDL web stream is accessible to VLC/browsers)\\n3. Click **Create Space**.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 3: Add Your Secrets (Environment Variables)\\n1. In your newly created Space, navigate to the **Settings** tab.\\n2. Scroll down to **Variables and secrets**.\\n3. Under **Secrets**, click **New secret** for each required key:\\n\\n| Secret Name | Value Example | Description |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| `API_ID` | `12345678` | From [my.telegram.org](https://my.telegram.org) |\\n| `API_HASH` | `abcdef123456789...` | From [my.telegram.org](https://my.telegram.org) |\\n| `BOT_TOKEN` | `1234567890:ABCdef...` | From `@BotFather` |\\n| `LOG_CHANNEL_ID` | `-1001234567890` | Your private storage channel ID |\\n| `MONGO_URI` | `mongodb+srv://...` | Free MongoDB Atlas connection string |\\n| `ALLOWED_USERS` | `123456789` | Your personal Telegram User ID |\\n| `STREAM_URL` | `https://<username>-stream-vault.hf.space` | Your Space's public HTTPS URL |\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Step 4: Push Your Code to Hugging Face\\nYou can connect Hugging Face directly to your existing GitHub repo or push with git:\\n\\n```powershell\\n# Add Hugging Face as a git remote (replace <username> with your HF username)\\ngit remote add hf https://huggingface.co/spaces/<your-username>/stream-vault\\n\\n# Push code to build and launch\\ngit push hf main --force\\n```\\n\\nHugging Face will automatically read the `Dockerfile`, install `ffmpeg`, `aria2c`, and launch your bot 24/7!\\n\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"Path\":\"d:\\\\Direct_Link\\\\docs\\\\huggingface-deploy.md\"}}]}\nconversations/session_02_movie_bot_architecture_explained/credentials-setup-guide.md:MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://user:pass@cluster.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority\ndocs/huggingface-deploy.md:| `MONGO_URI` | `mongodb+srv://...` | Free MongoDB Atlas connection string |\ndocs/setup-guide.md:     mongodb+srv://moviebot:<password>@cluster0.abcde.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority\ndocs/setup-guide.md:MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://moviebot:password@cluster0.abcde.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
