ver | **~0 MB** (Only tiny text queries) |\n| **Searching & Getting Links** | Bot sends text buttons in Telegram | **~0 MB** |\n| **Torrent Leeching via Google Colab** | Torrent ➔ Google Cloud ➔ Telegram | **0 MB** (Uses Google's cloud data) |\n| **Streaming/Watching the Movie** | Telegram ➔ Your Phone screen | Exactly the size of the movie (same as watching on Netflix/YouTube) |\n\n---\n\n### The Recommended Setup\n1. Keep the **bot and search indexer** running (it uses practically zero data, just a few kilobytes of text per day).\n2. Use **Google Colab** whenever you want to leech a torrent into your Telegram cloud for free without touching your mobile data.\n\nWould you like a ready-to-use 1-click **Google Colab notebook** for your cloud leeching?","thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nThe user's primary concern is excessive mobile data consumption when using a local leech bot. The core requirement is accessing movies directly on Telegram without incurring mobile data charges or needing paid solutions. Telegram channel scraping offers a solution: it avoids downloading files by only copying/forwarding from existing public channels, resulting in minimal data usage (kilobytes) for metadata transfer.\n\n\nChannel scraping avoids local downloads by copying/forwarding from public Telegram channels, minimizing data usage to metadata transfer, effectively using zero mobile data. Cloud debrid services like Seedr.cc or cloud VMs like GitHub Codespaces/Google Colab provide an alternative by downloading torrents or processing data within their cloud infrastructure, avoiding local bandwidth consumption. These cloud-based solutions ensure zero mobile data is used for downloading or uploading content.\n\n\n"}
