---\n\n### 🎯 The Best Real-World Combination\n* **Day-to-day (90% of movies):** Use your Telegram bot to search and get movies already on Telegram or under 2 GB (Seedr / YTS WebRips are usually 900 MB – 1.8 GB). Instant, zero effort.\n* **Heavy / 4K Movies (> 2 GB):** When you specifically want a massive 5 GB+ torrent, run the **Google Colab notebook** for 2 minutes to download, auto-split, and push it to your Telegram with zero hotspot data burned.\n\nWould you like me to create the **Google Colab notebook script (`leech_colab.ipynb`)** and push it to your repository so you have it ready to use anytime?","thinking":"Initial hypothesis: user needs a solution to download/handle files larger than 2GB, particularly video files, given the context of Seedr, Colab, and Telegram. Seedr's free tier is limited to 2GB, aligning with the user's implicit constraints. The user implicitly wants a solution to bypass the 2GB limit.\n\n\nThe user's implicit need is handling files exceeding 2GB, particularly video files, given constraints with Seedr's free tier. Telegram channels offer a workaround since uploaders manage file sizes, either by encoding under 2GB or splitting larger files using Telegram Premium, which the bot can then index. The key insight is that even free Telegram users can download files up to 4GB if someone else uploaded them with Premium, eliminating hotspot data usage.\n\nTorrent files exceeding 2GB are efficiently handled by Google Colab, which provides significant cloud disk space, RAM, and internet speed. Colab is capable of rapidly downloading and splitting large torrents for processing, circumventing the initial constraints.\n\n\nGoogle Colab offers the only 100% free, hotspot-data-free solution for torrents exceeding 2GB. Colab's ample cloud disk and RAM enable rapid torrent download and splitting into Telegram-compatible segments. Torrent files hosted on Telegram, even those exceeding 2GB uploaded by Premium users, are directly downloadable by standard fr