D (usually starts with `-100`, e.g. `-1002345678901`).\n6. 👉 **Copy and paste this into `.env` as `LOG_CHANNEL_ID`**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Get Your API_ID & API_HASH (Takes 2 min)\n1. Open your browser and go to: **[https://my.telegram.org](https://my.telegram.org)**.\n2. Enter your phone number (with country code, e.g. `+91...`).\n3. Telegram will send a confirmation code to your Telegram app. Enter it to log in.\n4. Click on **API development tools**.\n5. Type any App Title (e.g. `StreamVault`) and Short Name (e.g. `streamvault`).\n6. Click **Create application**.\n7. 👉 Copy **`App api_id`** into `.env` as `API_ID`.\n8. 👉 Copy **`App api_hash`** into `.env` as `API_HASH`.\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Free MongoDB Atlas Database (Takes 2 min)\n1. Go to **[mongodb.com/cloud/atlas/register](https://www.mongodb.com/cloud/atlas/register)** and sign up for free (or sign in with Google).\n2. Choose the **M0 Free (Shared)** tier.\n3. Click **Create Deployment**.\n4. Create a database user (e.g. Username: `admin`, Password: `Password123`).\n5. Under Network Access, choose **Allow Access from Anywhere** (`0.0.0.0/0`).\n6. Click **Connect** ➔ **Drivers** (Python) ➔ Copy the URI:\n   ```text\n   mongodb+srv://admin:<password>@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority\n   ```\n7. Replace `<password>` with the password you set in step 4.\n8. 👉 **Paste this into `.env` as `MONGO_URI`**.\n\n---\n\nLet me know once you have filled in these values (or if you get stuck on any step), and we will launch the bot and run our first channel indexing test!","thinking":"Focus shifts to the core components: Telegram Channel Scraper, AutoFilter Search, Storage Vault, and DDL Streaming. Leeching/torrent functionalities are deferred, marked as pending for future integration. Initial focus is on setting up the environment for the active modules.\n\n\nFocus now turns to updating the architecture plan to reflect the prioritized modules. The torrent-related modules will be explicitly marked