{"step_index":203,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-01T15:52:15Z","input_tokens":134428,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":1038,"content":"Select **Desktop** (or **Other**). \n\nTelegram does not restrict your keys based on platform—the `API_ID` and `API_HASH` will work identically for your Python bot regardless of which one you tap. **Desktop** is the most reliable choice that avoids form validation glitches on Telegram's site.\n\n---\n\n### Quick Form Checklist for `my.telegram.org`:\n* **App title:** `StreamVault`\n* **Short name:** `streamvault` *(only lowercase letters/numbers, no spaces or symbols)*\n* **URL:** Leave completely empty.\n* **Platform:** Select **Desktop** (or **Other**).\n* **Description:** Enter a short phrase:\n  ```text\n  Personal media backup and streaming client.\n  ```\n* Tap **Create application**.\n\n*(Note: If Telegram ever shows a red \"ERROR\", it's usually because the Description was left blank or the Short Name contained spaces/hyphens).*\n\n---\n\n### 👏 Great Progress!\nLooking at your other two screenshots:\n- You have already created **`@perso_streamvault_bot`**.\n- You have already successfully added it as an **Administrator** with full message rights in your private channel.\n\nOnce you click **Create application** on this page, copy your **`App api_id`** and **`App api_hash`** into your `.env` file!","thinking":"The request concerns the Telegram platform, specifically what to provide at \"my.telegram.org\". The images show an admin setup for \"My StreamVault\" bot and its associated registration. The user needs to know what to input during the registration process.\n\n\nThe platform field selection on `my.telegram.org` doesn't strictly limit API keys, but \"Bot / Server\" or a blank description can trigger errors. Recommending \"Desktop\" or \"Other\" as the platform, along with an app title, short name (lowercase and numbers only), empty URL, and a generic description, should work. Observing that the user's setup matches the suggested setup, it's ready to proceed to the next step.\n\n\n"}
