{"step_index":207,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-01T15:57:53Z","input_tokens":2447,"cache_read_tokens":137027,"output_tokens":923,"content":"Here are the quick steps from this screen:\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Name Your Project\n1. In the **Project Name** box, type:\n   ```text\n   stream-vault\n   ```\n2. Click the **Next** button (bottom right).\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Create the Project\n1. On the \"Add Members\" page that appears, simply click the green **Create Project** button (you don't need to add anyone).\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Deploy Free Database\nOnce the project opens:\n1. Click **Create a deployment** (or **Build a Database**).\n2. Choose the **M0 Free (Shared)** tier ($0/month).\n3. Leave provider and region as default (AWS is great).\n4. Click **Create Deployment** at the bottom.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Quick Security Setup (Username & Password)\nMongoDB will ask you to set up database access:\n1. **Username:** `admin` (or your name)\n2. **Password:** Type a password you remember (e.g. `StreamVault123`), then click **Create Database User**.\n3. **Where would you like to connect from?**\n   - Click **Allow Access from Anywhere** (it will set IP to `0.0.0.0/0`).\n4. Click **Finish and Close** (or **Go to Overview**).\n\n---\n\n### Step 5: Copy Your Connection String\n1. Next to your cluster, click the **Connect** button.\n2. Select **Drivers** (Python).\n3. Copy the URI string that looks like:\n   ```text\n   mongodb+srv://admin:<password>@cluster0.xxxxx.mongodb.net/?retryWrites=true&w=majority\n   ```\n4. Replace `<password>` with your password and paste it into `.env` as `MONGO_URI`!","thinking":"The user's request \"from this\" refers to the current state of a \"Create a Project\" screen. The interface elements indicate a project naming step. Focus is on a \"Project Name\" field, suggesting the next action is providing a project name. The \"Next\" button's greyed-out state implies a name is required before proceeding.\n\n\n"}
